messages:
jess: Heads-up: saw an SSE parse failure in the new sampleapp when a long event gets split across a reconnect. Node handler throws 'Unexpected end of JSON input'.

noah: which handler? are we using the same streaming helper across SDKs?

jess: src/stream/stream-parser.js in the node example. Repro is flaky but consistent with a net drop. Raw payloads show meta lines split:```
id: 101
retry: 3000
data: {"type":"update","chunk":"first part of a big blob"}

id: 102
data: {"type":"update","chunk":"second part"}
```
After reconnect we saw something like:```

data: {"type":"update","chunk":"second part"}
id: 103
```
which caused the parser to treat the leading newlines as an empty event and drop the `id` association.

sophia: hmm. In browser SDK we rely on the native EventSource which handles `\n\n` boundaries robustly. Node example uses a line-based split that assumes each chunk starts cleanly.

tyler: can you paste the parser code? Also include Node version and which lib you use for reconnects.

jess: parser snippet:```js
let buf = '';
function onChunk(chunk){
  buf += chunk.toString();
  const events = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = events.pop() || '';
  events.forEach(ev => {
    const lines = ev.split('\n');
    const meta = {};
    lines.forEach(l => {
      const [k,v] = l.split(': ');
      meta[k] = v;
    });
    if (meta.data) handle(JSON.parse(meta.data));
  });
}
```

noah: that split + naive k/v will break if `id:` or `data:` are split across buffers. and it assumes no leading blank lines.

sophia: We should adopt a streaming-state parser: process line-by-line (preserve partial line in buf), detect CRLF vs LF, and only treat a full blank line as event separator. Also preserve `id` from previous event if the server uses it for resume.

tyler: agree. Quick fix idea: when resuming, send `Last-Event-ID` header with the client's last good id, and on client reassembly, if the first thing is empty string, ignore it instead of turning into an event. But robust fix is incremental line parsing.

jess: I'll prototype incremental parser + add an integration test that injects a fake connection drop in the middle of a long `data:` line. Test should run in both node and the js-sdk harness.

noah: add `--sse-raw` flag to the sampleapp too so we can capture boundaries in CI when the test fails.

ci-bot: created issue #4129 for "sse: incremental parser + cross-sdk split-event regression test" and queued a small CI run for branch jess/fix-sse-split.

sophia: once PR is up, let's also run the browser + python parity suite. If we find discrepancies, log them to the streaming-parity epic.

jess: thanks all. I'll open the PR with changes: incremental parser, `--sse-raw` toggle, unit + netem integration test, and the failing payload captured. Will ping for reviews. :rocket:
